<p>What the manager actually holds is a vault: site passwords, and often notes, card numbers, and one-time codes. Check the current feature list before you assume a given type of item exists. The vault is encrypted. The company may store the ciphertext so your phone and your laptop can meet. Holding ciphertext is not the same as holding a list of readable passwords, and it is also not a reason to call the product beyond reach. A phishing page, a malware infection on an unlocked laptop, and a master password you also used on a forum are ordinary failures. None of them requires a dramatic break of the cipher.</p>
