<p>Even after data flows through the eSIM, a bank may text a code only to the home number. Check once, at a calm moment, where a code arrives before you switch that line off. If it does not arrive, see which line is selected for messages before you buy another package. Airplane mode sometimes brings up the wrong line after landing. Confirm that data points at the new profile and that home-line roaming is off if roaming was what you were leaving. Otherwise the calculator describes the purchase you typed, and the bill describes a different one.</p>
